From: Nura chopin port
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: allow direct firmware loading without an Android helper

Linux supplies connectivity firmware from the normal firmware search path.
Forcing the Android user-helper fallback makes optional missing configuration
files wait 60 seconds, exceeding the Wi-Fi power-on controller's timeout.
Let the kernel configuration select the firmware loader policy instead.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 
 menuconfig MEDIATEK_SOLUTION
 	bool "MediaTek Properitary Configuration"
-	select FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK
 	select I2C
 	help
 	  Check this to enable MediaTek properity configuration.
